What is Indium Phosphide (InP)?
Indium Phosphide (InP) is a critical III-V compound semiconductor material enabling high-speed, energy-efficient data transmission for AI computing infrastructure. It plays a pivotal role in optical communication systems, AI accelerators, and data center interconnects by overcoming the bandwidth limitations of traditional copper-based solutions. The material's superior electron mobility and direct bandgap make it exceptionally well-suited for photonic devices that power next-generation AI workloads, from large language model training to real-time inference in hyperscale facilities.
